== (1) Catalan numbers are the critical spine-block counts (q = 4, slope 1) ==
 positive min-ending words P_k, k = 1..15: [1, 0, 1, 0, 2, 0, 5, 0, 14, 0, 42, 0, 132, 0, 429]
 Catalan C_n at k = 2n+1 (odd k), 0 at even k: [1, 0, 1, 0, 2, 0, 5, 0, 14, 0, 42, 0, 132, 0, 429]
 positive words W_k: [1, 1, 2, 3, 6, 10, 20, 35, 70, 126, 252, 462, 924, 1716, 3432]  central binomials C(k-1, floor((k-1)/2)): [1, 1, 2, 3, 6, 10, 20, 35, 70, 126, 252, 462, 924, 1716, 3432]
 W = 1/(1 - P) (W_k = sum_j P_j W_(k-j)): True
 certification density at q = 4: fraction of length-k words that are NOT positive = 1 - C(k-1,floor((k-1)/2))/2^k; the
 non-certified fraction ~ sqrt(2/(pi k)): [0.123, 0.0398, 0.0126] vs [0.2523, 0.0798, 0.0252]
 C_n ~ 4^n n^(-3/2)/sqrt(pi): ratio C_n n^(3/2) sqrt(pi)/4^n at n = 10, 100, 500: [0.8978, 0.9889, 0.9978]
== (2) Catalan parity, Mersenne indices and the ternary condition ==
 n <= 4000 with C_n odd: [0, 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, 63, 127, 255, 511, 1023, 2047] ... = 2^k - 1: True
 n <= 4000 with C_n coprime to 6: [0, 1, 3, 31, 255]
 k <= 200 with 2^k - 1 free of the ternary digit 2 (a sum of distinct powers of 3): [1, 2, 5, 8] -> n = 2^k - 1 = [1, 3, 31, 255]
 (Kummer: v_3(C_n) = carries of n + n in base 3 minus v_3(n+1); no carries iff no ternary digit 2 in n)
 Erdos's conjecture concerns the ternary digits of 2^k (no digit 2 only for k = 0, 2, 8); here 2^k - 1, with k = 1, 2, 5, 8 below 200
